# Nexus contract

Nexus supports Cursor, Claude Code, Codex, and Hermes. Canonical release metadata lives in `release.json`. Follow `$using-nexus` (session bootstrap where hooks exist; Hermes uses profile `SOUL.md`). Procedures live in skills — do not invent workflows.

Nexus is a default layer. Precedence is: system and managed policy; explicit user instructions; host-native safety and approval controls; project instructions; Nexus; optional plugins and skills. When instructions at the same priority conflict, ask the user.

## Loop

1. Preferences — use session-injected preferences when present (global `~/.nexus/user/` plus repo `.nexus/user/`; repo overrides global on the same key); otherwise read both before workspace choice or closeout.
2. Workspace — `$git-assistant` → `workspace-choice` before first edit (`main` | named worktree).
3. Specify — `$spec-driven` before a feature or UI whose behavior, flow, or acceptance criteria are not already clear.
4. Act — smallest change; `$architect` before new files/modules.
5. Style — `$code-style` on touched files; React UI also uses `$frontend-quality`.
6. Review — `$integrity-review` on the affected area.
7. Closeout — on Clean/Corrected: `$git-assistant` → `closeout`; on Uncertain: stop.

## Routing

| Task | Skill |
| --- | --- |
| Bootstrap / skill discipline | `$using-nexus` |
| Git, workspace, closeout | `$git-assistant` |
| Final review | `$integrity-review` |
| Structure / placement | `$architect` |
| Style | `$code-style` |
| React | `$frontend` |
| Feature / UI specification | `$spec-driven` |
| React quality review | `$frontend-quality` |
| README | `$readme-writer` |
| Logs | `$log-writer` |
| Subagent coordination | `$subagent-guide` |
| Memory | `$memory` |
| Browser | `$playwright` |

## Hard gates

- No worktree, commit, merge to `main`, or push without approval for that step.
- Workflow artifacts: preference `commit workflow docs` = `include` | `exclude` | `ask` (default ask). `workflow docs paths` optionally defines the project-relative paths that receive this handling.
- No new automated test files unless asked; extend existing tests when needed.
- English for code/commits/harness docs; UI copy follows product language only when requested.
- Prefer uv for Python when the repo uses it; else local convention.
- Prefer current stable Python (3.13+) and stable Rust (edition 2024 when available, else 2021+) for greenfield; honor existing runtime pins.
- Naming: single-word files/modules preferred (two max); public before private; normalize only files you touch.
- Optional plugins may add workflows, but cannot override higher-priority instructions. Do not create a new test file, force a worktree, commit workflow artifacts, or install dependencies without an applicable project rule or user authorization.

## Memory

- Global: `~/.nexus/user/` preferences and `~/.nexus/notes/` (machine-wide; `$NEXUS_HOME` overrides root).
- Repo: `.nexus/user/` preferences (override global on the same key) and `.nexus/project/` learnings.
- Write only via `$memory` on explicit request. No secrets. Never store global memory in the Nexus plugin checkout.
